{"type":"text","timestamp":1790454716206,"sessionID":"ses_f209bd9a9ffefVPnGjMBWzfoS7","part":{"id":"prt_0df6ad71c0018K5GZtg4zduisP","messageID":"msg_0df6a0b90001DTaYNGdniSYg3Q","sessionID":"ses_f209bd9a9ffefVPnGjMBWzfoS7","type":"text","text":"**Maximum steps reached for this agent — tools are now disabled, so I'm summarizing the state of the work.**\n\n## What was accomplished\n\n1. **Explored the project**: `/workspace` is a Godot 4.4.1 project. `scenes/main.tscn` contains `Main` → `Trap` (Node2D at pos (320,180), scale (1.6,1.6)) → `Sprite2D` (tree_image.jpg, 3840×2160, sprite pos (64.5,34.5), scale (0.07473366, 0.08652595)).\n2. **Confirmed Godot works**: `godot --path . --quit-after 10 --write-movie` renders fine; captured the initial frame showing the tree against a blue background (water at the bottom of the screen).\n3. **Derived the coordinate mapping**: texture pixel → Trap-local coordinates:  \n   `local = (64.5 + tex_x*0.07473366, 34.5 + tex_y*0.08652595)`, where `tex = small_preview_px * 4`.\n4. **Analyzed the tree sprite** (with PIL + zoomed, grid-annotated crops in `/tmp/opencode/`):\n   - The lowest-drooping branch tip (\"branch closest to the water surface\") is in the region around small-preview coords ~(800, 430) → texture (~3200, 1720) → **Trap-local ≈ (303.6, 183.3)** (was still being refined in `cand_B.png`).\n   - A rightmost thin twig at the top (~(3772, 328) tex → local ≈ (346.5, 62.9)) was considered but is *higher*, so less likely the one \"closest to the water\".\n   - The zoom image for the trunk's rightmost bottom tip (`/tmp/opencode/cand_trunk.png`) was generated but not yet inspected; rough estimate from the overview: trunk's right-lower tip near texture (~2160, 2160) → **Trap-local ≈ (225.9, 221.4)** — this still needs visual confirmation.\n\n## What remains to be done\n\n1. Inspect `/tmp/opencode/cand_trunk.png` (and re‑check `cand_B.png`) to nail down the exact tip pixels.\n2. Edit `/workspace/scenes/main.tscn`, appending under the